# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev`. This file is the template and
# is committed; `.dev.vars` holds the real values and is not.
#
# This stack has no `.env`: a Worker's non-secret configuration lives in
# `wrangler.toml` [vars] and is deployed with the code, while `.dev.vars` is
# read by `wrangler dev` and ignored by `wrangler deploy`. So the split is not
# "public vs private" but "local vs deployed" -- the secrets below are set on
# the deployed Worker with `wrangler secret put`, never written to a file.

# Opens /v1/pubkey and /v1/dev/issue, and lets the service mint its own signing
# key. Local only -- never put this in wrangler.toml.
DEV_MODE = "1"
PUBLIC_BASE_URL = "http://localhost:8787"

# -- Paddle -------------------------------------------------------------------
# PADDLE_ENV is NOT set here. It lives in wrangler.toml [vars] because it must
# be identical for the deployed Worker and for local runs against the same
# account, and because the service now refuses to start a checkout when it is
# unset rather than assuming sandbox. See paddleEnvOrThrow in src/env.ts.
#
# Secrets, for local runs only. On the deployed Worker these are set with
# `wrangler secret put` and exist nowhere on disk. None of them is ever sent to
# the browser: PADDLE_API_KEY is used server-side for cancellations, customer
# lookup and minting customer portal sessions, and the only Paddle value that
# reaches the page is PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN, which is publishable by design.
PADDLE_API_KEY = "pdl_sdbx_apikey_..."
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET = "pdl_ntfset_..."

# -- Licence signing ----------------------------------------------------------
# Omit both locally and DEV_MODE mints an ephemeral pair on each run.
# SIGNING_KEY_PKCS8 = ""
# SIGNING_KEY_PUBLIC = ""

# -- Optional -----------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY = ""
# MAIL_FROM = "BubbleTranslate <no-reply@bubbletranslate.app>"
# ADMIN_PASSWORD = ""
